Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(TermCount);
define
    tcN=0;
    tcSink code={
        tcN = tcN + 1;
        };
    tcChild code={
        cerr "TCC " taG:;
        };
    tcRule code={
        cerr "TCR " taG:;
        iterate tcCur on argument;
        while ++tcCur;
            tcChild(*tcCur);
        };
    tcWalk code={
        iterate tcR on Grokking;
        while ++tcR;
            tcRule(*tcR);
        };
    ;
cerr "TCPHASE rest":;
tcWalk();
parser(Start);
tcSink(tcN);
cerr "TCPHASE after":;
tcWalk();
print "TERMCOUNT SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();

WHAT THIS IS

Object-model stroke 3's certificate (SEQ 220). It walks every Grokking rule's list twice -- at rest,
and again after parser(Start) plus one compiled action (tcSink) -- and prints each child's tag. pop.sh
counts in shell, never through a kant accessor (bear-trap 55).

THE CLAIM IS AN INVARIANT: artifacts no longer change a rule's term count, so the count at rest equals
the count after. Born red on trunk 0733d44: builtinParseR lands on 56 rules' lists at parser(Start),
and builtinActoR is on 33 at rest.

THE ANCHORS stop a walker that miscounts the same way twice from passing. Counted by hand from the
grammar lines: Braced 3 (leftBrace ExpressioN rightBrace, incant/grammar:130), Parens 3 (leftParen
ExpressioN? rightParen, :131), QuotE 2 (tik quoteBody, :44 -- and it carries an action, so today it
reads 3 at rest).
